<section class="tt-steps">
<div class="tt-container">
<div class="tt-steps-heading"><p class="tt-kicker">What participants learn</p><h2 class="tt-section-title">Practise PCM in four steps:</h2></div>
<div class="tt-step-grid">
<article class="tt-step"><div class="tt-step-visual"><img src="https://tujutaju.ee/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/pcm-how-it-works-02.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><h3>Be aware of your personality</h3><p>Understand your own preferences, psychological needs and the conditions that help you stay resourceful.</p></article>
<article class="tt-step"><div class="tt-step-visual"><img src="https://tujutaju.ee/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/pcm-how-it-works-03.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><h3>Recognise what others do, say and show</h3><p>Learn to notice observable patterns in words, tone, behaviour and reactions instead of relying only on assumptions.</p></article>
<article class="tt-step"><div class="tt-step-visual"><img src="https://tujutaju.ee/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/pcm-how-it-works-01-1.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><h3>Adapt your communication style</h3><p>Choose how to speak and respond so the message is easier for a different person to hear and use.</p></article>
<article class="tt-step"><div class="tt-step-visual"><img src="https://tujutaju.ee/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/pcm-how-it-works-04.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><h3>Build stronger relationships</h3><p>Use those skills in everyday conversations, meetings, feedback, pressure and difficult moments.</p></article>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="tt-how">
<div class="tt-container"><div class="tt-how-wrap">
<div><p class="tt-kicker">How training works</p><h2 class="tt-section-title">Theory only matters<br>when you can use it.</h2></div>
<div class="tt-how-list">
<article class="tt-how-item"><div class="tt-num">01</div><div><h3>Understand the model</h3><p>Participants get a clear, practical introduction to PCM and its core concepts.</p></div></article>
<article class="tt-how-item"><div class="tt-num">02</div><div><h3>Connect it to real situations</h3><p>Examples, discussions and exercises link the model to conversations participants already recognise from work.</p></div></article>
<article class="tt-how-item"><div class="tt-num">03</div><div><h3>Practise different responses</h3><p>The focus is not on memorising labels. It is on noticing more and having more options when communication matters.</p></div></article>
</div></div></div>
</section>

<section class="tt-formats">
<div class="tt-container">
<p class="tt-kicker">Training formats</p><h2 class="tt-section-title">Choose the depth that fits:</h2>
<div class="tt-format-grid">
<article class="tt-format-card"><h3>PCM Core Training</h3><p class="tt-sub">For teams and open groups</p><p>The full foundation of PCM: perception, communication channels, psychological needs and stress patterns.</p><p>It includes the official 26-page PCM personality profile.</p><p>A strong starting point for teams that want a common framework they can continue using after the training.</p><p class="tt-format-meta">16 hours · ET / EN / RU</p></article>
<article class="tt-format-card"><h3>PCM Leadership</h3><p class="tt-sub">For leaders and managers</p><p>The core model through a leadership lens: adapting communication, motivating different people and responding to stress more effectively.</p><p>Participants receive an extended Leadership Profile with additional material relevant to leading others.</p><p class="tt-format-meta"><a href="/leadership-training/">Leadership-focused programme</a></p></article>
<article class="tt-format-card"><h3>Advanced Training</h3><p class="tt-sub">For deeper practice</p><p>For people who already know the PCM foundations and want to deepen their ability to recognise patterns and use the model more precisely.</p><p>The focus moves from understanding the framework to using it with greater fluency.</p><p class="tt-format-meta">For previous PCM participants</p></article>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="tt-profile">
<div class="tt-container"><div class="tt-profile-wrap">
<div class="tt-profile-copy"><p class="tt-kicker">Individual profile</p><h2 class="tt-section-title"><span class="tt-title-line">A personal map</span><span class="tt-title-line">inside a shared model</span></h2><p>PCM training includes the official PCM personality profile. The standard profile is 26 pages and gives each participant a personal view of personality structure, communication preferences, psychological needs and stress patterns.</p><p>Leadership participants receive an extended profile with additional material relevant to leading others.</p></div>
<figure class="tt-profile-visual"><img class="tt-profile-image wp-image-2723" loading="eager" src="https://tujutaju.ee/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/IMG_2766-scaled.jpeg" alt="Example page from a personal PCM profile showing personality structure"><figcaption class="tt-profile-caption">26-page personal PCM profile</figcaption></figure>
</div></div>
</section>

<section class="tt-benefits">
<div class="tt-container"><div class="tt-benefits-panel">
<div class="tt-benefits-head"><div><p class="tt-kicker">How teams benefit</p><h2 class="tt-section-title">How PCM training supports teams</h2></div></div>
<div class="tt-benefit-track" id="ttBenefitTrack">
<article class="tt-benefit"><h3>Fewer conflicts</h3><p>Differences are recognised earlier, before they harden into personal tension.</p></article>
<article class="tt-benefit"><h3>Greater team comfort</h3><p>People have more ways to communicate without constantly pushing against each other.</p></article>
<article class="tt-benefit"><h3>Stronger mutual understanding</h3><p>Team members can make more sense of behaviour that previously felt confusing or frustrating.</p></article>
<article class="tt-benefit"><h3>More balanced participation</h3><p>Different communication styles have more room to contribute.</p></article>
<article class="tt-benefit"><h3>Stronger team stability</h3><p>A shared framework makes difficult periods easier to navigate together.</p></article>
<article class="tt-benefit"><h3>Increased satisfaction</h3><p>People are more likely to feel understood, respected and able to work in ways that suit them.</p></article>
</div>
