<section class="tt-hero"><div class="tt-container"><div class="tt-hero-grid"><div class="tt-hero-copy"><p class="tt-kicker">PCM WORKSHOP</p><h1>Six languages of communication</h1><p class="tt-hero-lead">What changes when you look at the same situation through six different perspectives? Try it together, and experience how much the way we communicate shapes what others hear.</p><p class="tt-hero-meta">In person · 1.5–2 hours · <span style="white-space:nowrap">12–18 participants · ET · EN · RU</span></p><a class="tt-button" href="mailto:contact@tujutaju.ee?subject=Six%20languages%20workshop">Ask about this workshop</a></div><figure class="tt-hero-photo"><img class="wp-image-2878" src="https://tujutaju.ee/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/PCM-Six-Keys-Tujutaju.webp" alt="PCM Six Keys Tujutaju" width="675" height="675"></figure></div></div></section>
<section class="tt-experience"><div class="tt-container"><div class="tt-experience-panel"><div class="tt-experience-intro"><p class="tt-kicker">How it works</p><h2 class="tt-section-title">Less lecture. More discovery.</h2><p>A short introduction gives the group just enough PCM to begin. Then everyone gets to try six ways of noticing and expressing a message. The difference becomes easier to understand when you experience it yourself.</p></div><div class="tt-experience-list"><div class="tt-experience-item"><span class="tt-experience-num" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>Try the six perspectives</h3><p>Move through a series of light, practical rounds. Each one invites a different way of looking at and describing a familiar topic.</p></div></div><div class="tt-experience-item"><span class="tt-experience-num" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>Notice what changes</h3><p>Some ways of speaking come easily. Others take more effort. Compare how the same message sounds when its focus shifts.</p></div></div><div class="tt-experience-item"><span class="tt-experience-num" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3>Connect it to real conversations</h3><p>Reflect together on what you noticed and where those differences show up with colleagues, clients and people close to you.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="tt-discover"><div class="tt-container"><p class="tt-kicker">What participants take away</p><h2 class="tt-section-title">One message can meet people in different ways</h2><div class="tt-discover-grid"><article class="tt-discover-card"><h3>A clearer sense of your own preferences</h3><p>Notice which ways of communicating come naturally to you, and which ones ask for a conscious change of perspective.</p></article><article class="tt-discover-card"><h3>More curiosity about other people</h3><p>See how the details one person notices first may be quite different from what matters to someone else.</p></article><article class="tt-discover-card"><h3>More options in a conversation</h3><p>When repeating the same message is not helping, changing how you express it can open a new point of connection.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="tt-details"><div class="tt-container"><div class="tt-details-grid"><div><p class="tt-kicker">The format</p><h2 class="tt-section-title">A practical session<br>for your group</h2><img class="tt-details-photo" src="https://tujutaju.ee/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/about-pcm-workshop-20261005.webp" alt="Participants practising communication together at Maia's workshop" width="1206" height="795" loading="lazy"></div><div class="tt-details-copy"><p>This workshop is for teams, leaders, teachers, professional communities and groups of friends who want to share the experience. No prior knowledge of Process Communication Model® is needed.</p><p>I choose familiar, low-pressure topics that suit your group, so participants can focus on the way they communicate rather than on solving a difficult scenario. The atmosphere stays lively and thoughtful, with time to compare observations afterwards.</p><div class="tt-details-facts"><div class="tt-fact"><strong>1.5–2 hours</strong><span>Time for practice and reflection</span></div><div class="tt-fact"><strong>12–18 people</strong><span>A group size for active participation</span></div><div class="tt-fact"><strong>In person</strong><span>In Tallinn or on site across Estonia</span></div><div class="tt-fact"><strong>ET · EN · RU</strong><span>Available in Estonian, English or Russian</span></div></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="tt-next"><div class="tt-container"><div class="tt-next-panel"><div><p class="tt-kicker">A first experience of PCM</p><h2 class="tt-section-title">A beginning you can experience</h2></div><div class="tt-next-copy"><p>This is a focused introduction, with space to experiment and notice differences in real time. It is not the full PCM training programme and does not include a personal profile.</p><p>If your group wants to go further afterwards, you can explore <a href="https://tujutaju.ee/pcm/">how PCM works</a> and the <a href="https://tujutaju.ee/trainings/">training formats</a>. The workshop also stands on its own as a useful shared experience.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="tt-cta"><div class="tt-container"><div class="tt-cta-panel"><div><h2 class="tt-section-title">Bring<br>the six languages<br>to your group</h2></div><div class="tt-cta-copy"><p>Tell me who will join and what kind of group you have.</p><p>We can choose the right setting and adapt the examples to make the session relevant to your people.</p><a class="tt-button" href="https://calendly.com/tujutaju/free-pcm-intro-call">Book a free 20-minute call</a></div></div></div></section>
</main>
